e and then one of the  biggest  bombs of the entire trailer is dropped  right here and no i'm not talking about  whatever is outside this window here  which is  kind of ominous looking i'm talking  about rabid  rosalina who looks just completely done  with life rabid rosalina  already being in this ship is kind of  strange to me it implies that there was  an adventure that has happened  before the events of what we see here  and it also implies  very specifically and very importantly  that rosalina does exist  in this universe somewhere we just can't  see her yet  or can we hold on for a sec so mario  tells rabbit rosalina get off your lazy  butt let's go have an adventure  and they walk out of the ship see and  then here  the ice rabbit luma flies above raven  rosalina implying once again that these  rabid  lumas are elemental power-ups for our  heroes looking at the rest of this  island that they landed on  it does confirm that this was that  island they were headed towards at the  first of  the trailer see the red autumn-like  leaves on these trees  they match the red autumn-like leaves on  these trees so the heroes are walking  outside  ready for a fight they turn around and  boom this never seen before luma  tiger giant enemy thing lands on top of  their ship  preventing them from leaving until they  defeat it the enemy itself is really  interesting looking but i don't think  it's anything more than just a strong  base level enemy because in the gameplay  trailer we can see them  fighting one of these enemies right off  the bat also this enemy's eyes are red  which i think is important because  when the other enemies start showing up  behind our heroes  we can see that their eyes are also red  not only does this give me some  really eerie like mind control super  smash ultimate vibes but that's probably  exactly what's happening because  it is heavily implied that they work for  this giant  faceless question mark hooded figure  with tentacles now we just saw a 